{"id":"s2.1.9","slug":"distance-velocity-conversions","title":"Distance and Velocity Conversions","content":"<p class=\"mb-4\">Memorizing key conversion factors for distance and velocity is essential. While some can be derived, having them ready saves time.</p><ul class=\"list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 mb-4\"><li>1 mile = 5280 ft</li><li>1 mile = 1760 yd</li><li>1 mile/hr = $\\frac{22}{15}$ ft/s</li><li>1 ft/min = $\\frac{1}{5}$ in/s</li><li>1 ft/hr = $\\frac{1}{5}$ in/min</li><li>1 mile/hr = $\\frac{88}{5}$ in/s</li><li>1 inch = 2.54 cm</li></ul>","summary":"Memorizing key conversion factors for distance and velocity is essential.","generation_guideline":"Generate a problem that requires converting between different units of distance or velocity.","questions":[{"id":1,"text":"15 miles per hour = ___ feet per second.","answer":"22","kind":"exact","tags":["conversions"]},{"id":2,"text":"3.5 yards = ___ inches.","answer":"126","kind":"exact","tags":["conversions"]},{"id":3,"text":".375 of a foot = ___ in.","answer":"4.5","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":4,"text":"48 inches per second = ___ ft/min.","answer":"240","kind":"exact","tags":["conversions"]},{"id":5,"text":"7.5 mph = ___ inches per second.","answer":"132","kind":"exact","tags":["conversions"]},{"id":6,"text":"$12\\frac{1}{2}\\%$ of a mile = ___ yards.","answer":"220","kind":"exact","tags":["fractions","percent","conversions"]},{"id":7,"text":"25% of a mile = ___ yards.","answer":"440","kind":"exact","tags":["percent","conversions"]},{"id":8,"text":"$\\frac{1}{3}$ of a mile = ___ feet.","answer":"1760","kind":"exact","tags":["fractions","conversions"]},{"id":9,"text":"$\\frac{3}{4}$ of 3 yards = ___ inches.","answer":"81","kind":"exact","tags":["fractions","conversions"]},{"id":10,"text":"$\\frac{2}{3}$ of a mile = ___ ft.","answer":"3520","kind":"exact","tags":["fractions"]},{"id":11,"text":"10 feet = ___ yards. (mixed number)","answer":"3 1/3","kind":"exact","requiredForm":"mixed","tags":["conversions"]},{"id":12,"text":"$83\\frac{1}{3}\\%$ of a foot = ___ inches.","answer":"10","kind":"exact","tags":["fractions","percent","conversions"]},{"id":13,"text":"30 mph = ___ ft/sec.","answer":"44","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":14,"text":"30 feet per minute = ___ feet per second.","answer":"0.5","kind":"exact","tags":["conversions"]},{"id":15,"text":"36 in/s = ___ inches per minute.","answer":"2160","kind":"exact","tags":["conversions"]},{"id":16,"text":"480 inches per minute = ___ in/s.","answer":"8","kind":"exact","tags":["conversions"]},{"id":17,"text":"45 mph = ___ ft/s.","answer":"66","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":18,"text":"33 ft/s = ___ mph.","answer":"22.5","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":19,"text":"7.5 mph = ___ ft/s.","answer":"11","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]}]}